<div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
      		
	<p n="1-2">
		Eleventh year the victorious king Mayēntiraparumaṉ.<note>Sanskrit Mahendravarman.</note>		
	</p>
	
	<p n="2-8">
		 Ēṟaṉ, the younger son <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>iḷa-makaṉ</foreign></supplied> of Cākkai Paraiyaṉār, the servant of Amkōṭṭaiyār, the nephew <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>maru-makkaḷ</foreign></supplied> of Perumpōttaraiyar,
		attacked <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>eṟintu</foreign><note>Literally: having attacked.</note></supplied> and died,
		when Vilakkumiṟaiyar marched upon <supplied reason="subaudible">the village of</supplied> Tuṭari in Kīḻvēṇāṭu.
	</p>
	
</div>
      	
